    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d248">

                <pb facs="0471" n="185" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg185"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2397</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-01T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1916, 2 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2757. German memorandum and appendices regarding submarine policy and armed
                    merchantmen not yet received. Just when may they be expected? Can you say on
                    what steamship they were sent?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
